## Why This Is Asked
Tests mastery of graph algorithms, state expansion techniques, and path reconstruction under constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Dijkstra's algorithm on expanded state space (node, used)
- Edge relaxation with and without discount application
- Path reconstruction across state transitions

## Code Example
```javascript
function shortestWithDiscounts(n, edges, s, t, K) {
  const adj = Array.from({length: n}, ()=>[]);
  for(const [u,v,w] of edges){ adj[u].push([v,w]); }
  const INF = Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY;
  const dist = Array.from({length: n}, ()=> Array(K+1).fill(INF));
  const prev = Array.from({length: n}, ()=> Array(K+1).fill(null));

  const pq = new MinHeap();
  dist[s][0] = 0;
  pq.insert([s,0,0]); // [node, used, distance]

  while(!pq.isEmpty()){
    const [u,used,d] = pq.extractMin();
    if(d > dist[u][used]) continue;
    if(u === t) break;

    for(const [v,w] of adj[u]){
      // Without discount
      if(d + w < dist[v][used]){
        dist[v][used] = d + w;
        prev[v][used] = [u,used];
        pq.insert([v,used,d+w]);
      }
      // With discount if available
      if(used < K && d < dist[v][used+1]){
        dist[v][used+1] = d;
        prev[v][used+1] = [u,used];
        pq.insert([v,used+1,d]);
      }
    }
  }

  // Find optimal state at target
  let minDist = INF, minUsed = -1;
  for(let k=0;k<=K;k++){
    if(dist[t][k] < minDist){
      minDist = dist[t][k];
      minUsed = k;
    }
  }

  // Path reconstruction
  const path = [];
  let curr = [t,minUsed];
  while(curr && prev[curr[0]][curr[1]]){
    path.unshift(curr[0]);
    curr = prev[curr[0]][curr[1]];
  }
  if(curr[0] === s) path.unshift(s);

  return {distance: minDist, path};
}
```

## Edge Cases
- Unreachable target: return INF distance
- K=0: reduces to standard Dijkstra
- K larger than path length: effectively unlimited discounts
- Multiple optimal states: choose minimal used count

## Why This Question Is Asked

This problem tests your ability to combine multiple data structures to solve a real-world analytics challenge: maintaining sliding window aggregations with fast top-K retrieval under tight latency constraints.

## Key Concepts

1. **Circular bucket array** enables O(1) bucketing and automatic expiration of old events
2. **Hashmap aggregation** provides O(1) lookup and update for per-user totals across categories
3. **Max-heap with lazy deletion** avoids the overhead of rebuilding the heap on every expiration; stale entries are filtered on-demand during `topK`
4. **Lazy expiration** ensures we never scan individual events during query time—only expired buckets trigger cleanup

## Code Example

```javascript
class WindowedTopK {
  constructor(W) {
    this.W = W;
    this.buckets = new Array(W).fill(null).map(() => ({ head: null, tail: null, ts: null }));
    this.totals = new Map();
    this.heap = [];
    this.head = 0;
  }

  insertEvent(ts, userId, category, value) {
    const idx = ts % this.W;
    const bucket = this.buckets[idx];
    const event = { userId, category, value, ts, next: null };
    if (!bucket.head) bucket.head = bucket.tail = event;
    else bucket.tail = bucket.tail.next = event;
    bucket.ts = ts;

    this.totals.set(userId, (this.totals.get(userId) || 0) + value);
    this.heap.push({ total: this.totals.get(userId), userId, ts });
  }

  advanceTime(now) {
    const cutoff = now - this.W;
    while (this.buckets[this.head].ts !== null && this.buckets[this.head].ts < cutoff) {
      let event = this.buckets[this.head].head;
      while (event) {
        this.totals.set(event.userId, (this.totals.get(event.userId) || 0) - event.value);
        event = event.next;
      }
      this.buckets[this.head] = { head: null, tail: null, ts: null };
      this.head = (this.head + 1) % this.W;
    }
  }

  topK(now, K) {
    this.advanceTime(now);
    const result = [];
    let i = 0;
    while (result.length < K && i < this.heap.length) {
      const entry = this.heap[i++];
      if (this.totals.get(entry.userId) === entry.total) {
        result.push(entry.userId);
      }
    }
    return result;
  }
}
```

